  "emma": {
    "route": "/history/emma-hale-smith.html",
    "stories": [
      {
        "base": "emma-story1-ride-review",
        "key": "emma-story1-ride",
        "figure": "#picture-emma-story1-ride",
        "fragment": "#picture-emma-story1-ride",
        "section": "#elect-lady-right-person",
        "alt": "Emma Smith at twenty three, wearing a long blue dress, rides sidesaddle at a gallop on a brown horse up a leaf covered slope in autumn, leaning forward with both hands on the reins and her eyes on the path ahead.",
        "title": "A ride to warn Joseph",
        "sourceHref": "https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/liahona/2021/03/emma-protected-scripture?lang=eng",
        "requiredText": "In the first hours of September 22, 1827, Joseph Smith prepared to go to the hill where the gold plates were buried. The angel Moroni had told him to bring the right person with him, and Joseph knew through personal revelation that the right person was Emma. She waited while he received the plates and hid them in a hollow log, and she rode home beside him as the sun rose. From the very first night of the work, Emma was not watching from a distance. She was in the carriage.",
        "referenceRoute": "/history/emma-elect-lady.html",
        "referenceSelector": "figure.fc-reference-picture[data-artwork-reference] > div > a[href=\"emma-hale-smith.html#picture-emma-story1-ride\"]",
        "referenceHref": "emma-hale-smith.html#picture-emma-story1-ride"
      },
      {
        "base": "emma-story2-hymnal-review",
        "key": "emma-story2-hymnal",
        "figure": "#picture-emma-story2-hymnal",
        "fragment": "#picture-emma-story2-hymnal",
        "section": "#hymns-book",
        "alt": "Emma Smith at thirty one, wearing a brown dress, stands by a window holding a small bound book in both hands and looking down at it.",
        "title": "The finished hymnbook",
        "sourceHref": "https://www.josephsmithpapers.org/paper-summary/collection-of-sacred-hymns-1835/1",
        "requiredText": "The first Latter-day Saint hymnbook was prepared at Kirtland: A Collection of Sacred Hymns for the Church of the Latter Day Saints. The edition is dated 1835, and its title page names the hymns as selected by Emma Smith. The printing ran late, though. The Joseph Smith Papers, which publishes the book, notes that although it bears an 1835 date it was apparently not available until early 1836. It held ninety hymn texts and no musical notation at all, just words, gathered so that families and branches who had no songbook and perhaps no instrument could still carry the tunes they knew and learn new ones. The little book traveled where the Saints traveled, into homes and small meeting rooms, and it treated singing as something the whole church did together, not something performed for them.",
        "referenceRoute": "/history/emma-hymns.html",
        "referenceSelector": "figure.fc-reference-picture[data-artwork-reference] > div > a[href=\"emma-hale-smith.html#picture-emma-story2-hymnal\"]",
        "referenceHref": "emma-hale-smith.html#picture-emma-story2-hymnal",
        "reader": {
          "selector": ".fc-artwork-detail-copy a.fc-inline-scripture[href=\"https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/dc-testament/dc/25?lang=eng\"]",
          "href": "https://www.churchofjesuschrist.org/study/scriptures/dc-testament/dc/25?lang=eng",
          "title": "Doctrine and Covenants 25",
          "numbers": [
            1,
            2,
            3,
            4,
            5,
